{"requirements":[{"id":"schedule","requirement":"Configure node1 to run /usr/local/bin/inventory-maintenance daily at 02:15.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A root-owned, mode-0644 cron.d entry specifies `15 2 * * *`, passes Cron syntax validation, and remains present with crond active and enabled after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-768cf52d3e6c46be","cmd-bfab2d3e82774a89","cmd-d033bd1300ff45ba"]},{"id":"output-retention","requirement":"Append the maintenance command's output to /var/log/inventory-maintenance.log.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The Cron command redirects both stdout and stderr to the requested log. Scheduler-like executions before and after restart appended distinct records, while the pre-restart record persisted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1d682c0a8b1c44e0","cmd-bfab2d3e82774a89","cmd-d033bd1300ff45ba"]},{"id":"platform-preservation","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The system remained RHEL 10.0 on kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 before and after execution and restart. The executor used the existing active Cron implementation without installing or changing software.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a4a7ae08c2404d07","cmd-bfab2d3e82774a89","cmd-d033bd1300ff45ba","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The Cron installation and SELinux labeling in cmd-768cf52d3e6c46be established the requested schedule; cmd-1d682c0a8b1c44e0 created and labeled the required log while validating output capture; cmd-51dbe96e5905467f initiated the mandatory restart protocol through transient state removed by reboot; and cmd-d033bd1300ff45ba performed bounded post-restart validation that appended one legitimate test record. The temporary installation file was removed by its trap. Final snapshots show no failed services, damaged package state, new exposure, or abandoned temporary files; observed temporary-directory and socket PID changes are normal consequences of the verified reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-768cf52d3e6c46be","cmd-1d682c0a8b1c44e0","cmd-51dbe96e5905467f","cmd-d033bd1300ff45ba","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for node1: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged and accompanied by loss of connectivity, the post-restart boot ID changed, and the Cron service, schedule, retained log data, platform, and command execution recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":["No naturally timed 02:15 Cron firing was captured; correct daily scheduling is established through the installed syntax-valid entry, active/enabled crond, and scheduler-like execution tests."]}
